From: Domenico D'Arrigo <d.darrigo@outlook.it>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 11:22:45 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] UefiPayloadPkg: The HSTI of the platform

Publish the Hardware Security Testability Interface: when a boot is
started, after the platform has armed its locks, read the flash
protections (FLOCKDN, BIOS_CNTL, the Protected Ranges, the descriptor
and ME region access), the TSEG lock, the debug interface lock, the
microcode, Secure Boot, the TPM, the setup option lock and the MOR lock,
and publish the result as the HSTI table of the Adapter Information
protocol, with role IBV, and as the volatile variable HstiTable of the
same GUID, read-only for the OS (Variable Policy, lock on create).

A test that fails is reported as such, with a line in the error string:
the table tells what the platform does not have (a descriptor the host
cannot write, pre-boot DMA protection) as well as what it has.
---
